# Symbols accepted as intentional/benign clashes by check_symbol_clashes.sh.
#
# One symbol per line, optionally followed by whitespace and a reason. Lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# This list only suppresses the "external data symbol shadows libpd" failure
# (the class of bug that made ggee's slider_widgetbehavior crash Pd's built-in
# [hsl]/[vsl] classes). Function duplicates and external-vs-external
# duplicates are reported, never failed, so they do not need entries here.
#
# Currently empty on purpose: ggee's slider_widgetbehavior is made file-local
# by ggee-widgetbehavior-static.patch, and the remaining libpd function
# duplicates (cyclone's and ELSE's u8_* copies) are the exact same upstream
# code and harmless with -Wl,-Bsymbolic.
#
# Example:
#   some_symbol   comment explaining why the clash is accepted
